# Claude Code & Codex: allowlist-only (defense in depth).
# These dirs hold credentials (~/.codex/auth.json), session transcripts,
# sqlite state, caches, telemetry and memories that must never reach this
# PUBLIC repo. Ignore each dir's contents, then re-include ONLY the files
# chezmoi is meant to manage. chezmoi honors .chezmoiignore during
# `chezmoi add`, so this also blocks accidental recursive ingestion of
# secrets/state (e.g. an errant `chezmoi add ~/.codex`).
#
# NB: gitignore/chezmoi cannot re-include a file under an ignored directory,
# so ignore one level at a time (dir/*) and re-include each parent dir we
# need to descend into — NOT dir/** (which ignores the dirs themselves).
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/statusline.sh
!.claude/subagent-statusline.sh
!.claude/git-forge-guard.sh
!.claude/worktree-guard.sh
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/sp-mechanical.md
!.claude/agents/sp-standard.md
!.claude/agents/sp-architect.md
!.claude/themes/
.claude/themes/*
!.claude/themes/tokyo-night.json

.codex/*
!.codex/AGENTS.md
!.codex/config.toml
!.codex/themes/
.codex/themes/*
!.codex/themes/tokyo-night.tmTheme

# Alfred: allowlist-only, same reasoning as above. Only the cross-model relay snippet
# collection belongs in this PUBLIC repo. The rest of the preferences bundle holds
# workflow configuration, which routinely contains API keys and tokens, plus clipboard
# history and machine-local state. Descend one level at a time — a re-include cannot
# reach inside an ignored directory.
Library/Application Support/Alfred/*
!Library/Application Support/Alfred/Alfred.alfredpreferences/
Library/Application Support/Alfred/Alfred.alfredpreferences/*
!Library/Application Support/Alfred/Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/
Library/Application Support/Alfred/Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/*
!Library/Application Support/Alfred/Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Relay/
